<BaseLayout title="About Which Deal's Better?" description="Why Which Deal's Better connects unit-price comparisons, discount math, private usage history, and stock-up estimates without retailer influence.">
  <section class="content-section"><div class="shell prose"><p class="eyebrow">About the toolkit</p><h1>Shopping math for the decision in front of you.</h1><p>Which Deal's Better? exists for the moment when sticker prices, package sizes, and sale language point in different directions. A cheaper package can contain less. A bigger discount can produce a higher final price. A bulk deal can be economical per unit and still be more than a household will use.</p><h2>How the tools work together</h2><p><a href="/">Compare Deals</a> normalizes amounts, multipacks, and compatible units. The <a href="/coupon-comparator/">Coupon Comparator</a> works from final checkout prices. If you choose, the <a href="/usage-tracker/">Usage Tracker</a> records how long a purchase lasts, and the <a href="/stock-up-calculator/">Stock-Up Calculator</a> can use that selected history to estimate supply duration.</p><p>The goal is transparent decision support, not a recommendation from a retailer. The site does not retrieve offers, rank brands, or earn a different result based on which store or product wins.</p><h2>No account required</h2><p>Calculations happen in your browser. Usage records remain in local storage on this device unless you delete them or clear browser data. The optional “Track this purchase” action uses browser session storage to carry a winning deal into the tracker without putting item details in a URL.</p><h2>Know what the number leaves out</h2><p>Lowest unit price is useful, but it does not measure shelf life, storage, product quality, cash available today, or coupon eligibility. The site shows its formulas and limitations in the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> so you can decide which factors matter for your purchase.</p><p><a class="primary-button" href="/">Compare deals now</a></p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
